tests:
  unit:
    count: 0
    waived: "The WU touches no product code or screens — the E-DFLOW.W9 precedent the epic plan cites for design WUs (W1, W3, W5, W7, W9), and the same waiver W1 carried. The diff is two HTML documents under docs/work/; ui/src/ and src/ are untouched, so there is nothing for a unit to assert against. The design's claims become assertions in W6, beside the .tsx: that the copy confirm reverts (the sticky-copied defect this run names at FlowDetail.tsx:58-61), that an empty leg renders Notice rather than a bare word, that the verb carries MethodLabel's tone, and that Esc closes the panel."
  integration:
    count: 0
    waived: "Same precedent. There is no bounded contract in code to exercise: the contract this WU produces IS the run document, and cargo xtask verify-doc is what judges its shape — 17/17 soft rules receipted against the rulebook on disk, 13/13 hard rules machine-checked, every reuse verdict mounted rather than drawn."
  e2e:
    count: 0
    waived: "Same precedent, and it holds here in a way it did not for W2: no user-visible surface moves. FlowDetail.tsx is not touched by this diff — the run designs its replacement, it does not build it. UC-5's e2e runs against the built screen in W6. (W2's identical waiver was voided at review because the fix migrated three screens; this diff contains no code at all, so that failure mode cannot arise. Verified across BOTH commits: git diff --stat 42875df..HEAD lists five documentation files and nothing else — the three docs/work/ files (the two this WU adds plus the epic plan, whose W7/W8 rows the review's blocker required this WU to correct) and the two docs/decisions/ files carrying DEC-31 and its index row.)"
verified:
  - "cargo xtask verify-doc docs/work/2026-09-04-redesign-w5-flow-detail-run.html — green (design-run). receipt 17/17 soft · 14 satisfied · 2 inherited · 1 blocked. hard rules 13/13 machine-checked. design-allow: 0 live suppressions. Run archived AFTER green, per the flow spec's step order — an earlier draft was marked archived before it had ever been verified, at which point the checker skipped it entirely and reported neither pass nor fail; reopening it surfaced 22 real failures across two batches. A design run marked archived without a prior green is unverified, not verified."
  - "cargo xtask verify-doc docs/work/2026-09-04-redesign-w5-plan.html — green (wu-plan)."
  - "node scripts/check-render.mjs on the run — ok, 4 mounts, 5 buttons, clean console, opened over file:// with no flags. This is the gate that matters for a mockup: verify-doc proves components are MOUNTED, not that they RENDER. It caught a real ReferenceError (SegmentedControl missing from the window.Trawler destructure) that left the panel silently blank while every static check stayed green."
  - "Live behaviour, in headless Chrome rather than asserted in prose: clicking the response segment swaps the header table (aria-label 'response headers', first key content-type) AND the body stub ('response body'), while the URI is UNCHANGED. That is the flow-scoped/leg-scoped split of Tune 9 actually working, and it is the claim the run would otherwise only be making in words."
  - "git hash-object docs/design-rules/design-rules-index.html = aeff5b0fb4dea94ab5f0b7c385b8188786666e8a, re-checked at close against the receipt's pin — the rulebook did not move under the run (receipt·rulebook-stale clean)."
  - "node scripts/design-registry.mjs — 27 entries, read once at the start and frozen for the run."
  - "git diff --stat 42875df..<tip> — five files, all under docs/, 0 lines of src/ or ui/src/. This is the evidence behind all three waivers, measured across the whole WU rather than one commit."
  - "THREE Tier-3 review rounds, each on its own tip, each finding real defects. Round 1 (f621253): 9 verified — a blocker (the epic plan's W7 row still promising a leg switch W5 deleted, justified by a workflow rule that does not exist), two wrong Section counts, a wrong rule slug in the review narrative, five wrong file:line citations, a wrong distillation citation. Round 2 (934307b): 8 more — the W8 half of the epic-plan fix was CLAIMED in three artifacts and never applied (a replacement matching whitespace the file does not contain, failing silently), four more citations in a shorthand form the first fix pass never checked, an orphan zone reference that survived three restructures, two dead CSS rules, and a rejected 'no DEC' justification that borrowed a threshold from the wrong checklist row. Round 3 (ca18daa): 4 — two blockers of my own making (the notes were never carried to the tip, leaving a standing doc/v1 that contradicted the DEC-31 this WU had just opened), an index ordering defect, and a blocked-on row that linked to DEC-31 and then restated it. Across all three rounds ~15 further candidates were refuted at verification — the largest being a claim that all 8 States cells illegally re-list component states, refuted because the flow spec's own template reads <per its design file (cite it)> and the cells cite rather than enumerate."
  - "Every citation in both documents re-verified line by line against the source at the final tip, in BOTH forms — the File.tsx:N form and the bare <code>:N</code> shorthand. The shorthand is what round 2 caught: fixing only the prefixed form left four wrong."
note: "A design WU: the deliverable is a judged document, so the pyramid is waived at all three levels and the real gates are verify-doc, the render gate and the Tier-3 design review. Three reviewer rounds materially reshaped the artifact and two of them corrected ME, which the run records rather than smooths away. Round 2 reversed my refusal of a leg switch: I had weighed it against a goal 4 phrased as 'compare the two legs' and never checked whether the panel already contradicted that — BodyViewer ships its own request/response toggle (BodyViewer.tsx:148, :196-201), so the screen already had two models of one concept. Round 3 found three faults with one cause, including a 'Request' heading I had introduced in round 2 that never followed the selector. Two receipt verdicts are deliberately NOT satisfied: keyboard-parity and focus-returns-to-origin are blocked, because Esc is designed per the rulebook's own sighting on this exact panel but FlowDetail binds no key handler — a designed path is not a shipped one, and satisfied there would be precisely the complete-fluent-and-false receipt the Tier-3 review exists to catch. One seam moved: leg selection is now the panel's, so W7's leg switch is deleted rather than redesigned and its run shrinks to the decode toggle, the dispatch and the absences. An earlier draft of this WU asserted that W5 may not edit W7's plan row and left the consequence in blocked-on only — no such rule exists in the workflow, and W2's precedent (d7f186c) is the opposite. Found at the Tier-3 review: the epic plan's W7 and W8 rows are corrected in this WU, and the rule itself is distilled to DEC-31."
